# Build context filter for the APPLICATION image (Dockerfile at the repo root).
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here ships inside
# the public image that people self-host. Two rules follow from that:
#   1. Credentials must never be in the context -- a local `docker build .` runs
#      against a working tree that holds a real .env.
#   2. Anything that is not the application itself stays out, so self-hosters
#      get the app and nothing else.
# tests/test_autoscaler.py asserts the entries below still exist.

# --- Credentials: never in an image layer ---
.env
.env.*
env/

# --- Version control ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --- Swarm operations tooling: infrastructure, not application ---
ops/

# --- Tests and dev tooling ---
tests/
requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache/
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Project documentation and meta (assets/markdown/ is app content, kept) ---
docs/
README.md
CLAUDE.md
PRIVACY.md
SECURITY.md

# --- Orchestration files: the image is orchestrator-agnostic ---
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Python and tooling caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
